From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio Naganohara <mio@meow.business>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: use /tmp as TMPDIR in shell sessions on standalone Linux

Upstream hardcodes Android's /data/local/tmp, which does not exist on a
standalone Linux rootfs -- anything honoring $TMPDIR (mktemp, editors,
downloaders) breaks inside `adb shell`. Point it at /tmp instead.
---
 daemon/shell_service.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/daemon/shell_service.cpp b/daemon/shell_service.cpp
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/daemon/shell_service.cpp
+++ b/daemon/shell_service.cpp
@@ -279,7 +279,11 @@ bool Subprocess::ForkAndExec(std::string* error) {
         env["HOSTNAME"] = GetHostName();
         env["LOGNAME"] = pw->pw_name;
         env["SHELL"] = shell_path;
+#if defined(ADB_STANDALONE_LINUX)
+        env["TMPDIR"] = "/tmp";
+#else
         env["TMPDIR"] = "/data/local/tmp";
+#endif
         env["USER"] = pw->pw_name;
     }
 
-- 
2.54.0
